course: dictionary
lesson: 14161
title: Mistreatment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mistreatment is a noun. It means treating a person or an animal cruelly or unfairly, for example by hurting them, starving them or not caring for them.
explain: Use the clues in a sentence. «The dog had suffered mistreatment, so the rescue centre took it in.» The word suffered tells you the dog was harmed by bad treatment. If you swap in "bad treatment" and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: In lessons about safety and animals, mistreatment is something to report to a trusted adult. In the UK you can also contact the RSPCA, a charity that helps animals. «Report mistreatment» means telling someone who can help stop it.
fact: Mistreatment means cruel or unfair treatment of a person or an animal.
fact: «Mistreatment of animals» is a common phrase. It can include hurting animals, starving them or not caring for them.
fact: «Suffer mistreatment» means to be treated cruelly or unfairly and to feel the harm of it.
fact: If you see mistreatment, tell a trusted adult. In the UK, you can also contact the RSPCA.
fact: Mistreatment is an uncountable noun, so we say «some mistreatment», not «a mistreatments».
exercise: «The rescue centre helped the dog recover from years of mistreatment.» What does mistreatment mean here? | Being given too much food | *Cruel or unfair treatment | Long walks in the park | A fun new toy
exercise: «Please report any mistreatment to a trusted adult.» What should you do if you see mistreatment? | Join in to be friendly | Ignore it because it is none of your business | Keep it secret | *Tell a trusted adult
exercise: Which phrase means cruelty to animals? | Feeding time at the zoo | Animal shelter open day | *Mistreatment of animals | Care of animals
test: Which group could you contact in the UK to report mistreatment of an animal? | *The RSPCA | The library | The weather office | The bus company
test: Which sentence uses mistreatment correctly? | Mistreatment is a type of cake we eat at breakfast. | The mistreatment was sweet and sunny. | *Workers had suffered mistreatment for years. | Mistreatment is a fast running shoe.
exam: What is the best meaning of mistreatment? | *Cruel or unfair treatment of a person or animal | A type of weather | A kind way of helping someone | Being very tired after school
